@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@ Expected provider failures return a structured, model-visible error envelope wit
 terminating the agent stream.
 
 For separate image and video routes, configure named providers. Built-in adapters cover Volcengine Ark
-(Seedream/Seedance), Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (Wan), and MiniMax (image-01/H3):
+(Seedream/Seedance), Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (Wan), MiniMax (image-01/H3), and OpenAI Images (GPT Image):
 
 ```python
 from octop_harness import HarnessAgentConfig, MediaGenerationConfig, MediaProviderConfig
@@ -214,6 +214,23 @@ config = HarnessAgentConfig(
 )
 ```
 
+For OpenAI Images, use the `openai_images` protocol with `OPENAI_API_KEY` (or an injected `api_key`):
+
+```python
+images = MediaProviderConfig(id="openai-images", provider="openai_images")
+# Defaults: https://api.openai.com/v1 and gpt-image-2.
+# Use images in MediaGenerationConfig(providers=[images, ...]) alongside a video provider.
+```
+
+`OpenAIImagesMediaProvider` sends text-only requests to `/images/generations` and reference-image edits
+to `/images/edits` as multipart uploads. Local paths, HTTP(S) URLs, and base64 data URLs are supported
+as references; edits accept up to 16 PNG, JPEG, or WebP images (each must satisfy OpenAI's 50 MB limit).
+GPT Image base64 responses are decoded into normal workspace image artifacts. The adapter requests PNG
+output and forwards prompt, count, and optional size; shared seed and watermark options are not forwarded.
+It automatically disables video in both single-provider and named-provider configuration; selecting it
+for video is rejected, while other providers keep their video routes. Low-level `MediaManager.add_provider`
+callers must pass `video_enabled=False` when registering this adapter.
+
 Advanced hosts can inject a `MediaManager` into `build_media_generation_tools` and register a constrained
 custom adapter without adding arbitrary protocol or authentication fields to declarative configuration.
 
